  "summary": "A Goodyear, AZ police audit of Flock ALPR activity flagged misuse by an officer, who was placed on leave and later resigned in September before the investigation concluded. The department found three policy violations (abuse of authority, body-worn camera policy, dishonesty) and the chief said he would have fired the officer. The article notes similar ALPR misuse resignations at Apache Junction and Chandler PDs and Tempe's recent ban.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "During a routine audit of Flock automated license plate reader (ALPR) activity in July, internal affairs flagged a possible violation of department policy.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Based on the findings of this investigation, I would have upheld the termination of this officer had he remained employed by the Goodyear Police Department.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "An Apache Junction officer resigned in August after investigators said he used Flock cameras to track his wife. Days later, a Chandler officer resigned for reportedly using the system to track a family member.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
